  "limitations": "The theorem classifies exact equality in the quadratic NOC bound but does not give stability for near-extremal systems or enumerate all NOC systems. The n!/2 network counts apply to the two canonical normal-network classes covered by the cited bijections, not to arbitrary non-regular realizations. Older set-system literature under different terminology and very recent unindexed work remain residual originality risks. Finite computation supports but does not replace the proof. No independent validation is asserted.",
